 "story": {
  "title": "Wheat waltzes, rice bounces",
  "lede": "Punjab's fields grow wheat in winter and rice in the monsoon. NISAR watched both, and the two crops move in completely different ways.",
  "body": [
   "Wheat is a volume dance. As the canopy grows, leaves scatter the radar in every direction and HV climbs about 3 dB, from late November to February. Harvest in April drops the fields back to bare soil.",
   "Rice is a bounce. Seedlings are planted into flooded paddies in July. By September the stalks stand in water, the pulse bounces off the water and up the stalks, and the median HH jumps about 7 dB while HV rises far less. The gap between HH and HV widens from about 9 dB to 12 dB: the double-bounce fingerprint.",
   "Medians over about 70,000 cultivated hectares in a 29 by 29 km box near Ludhiana."
  ],
